.TH LOD.QOS_MAXAGE 4 2026-09-29 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
lod.qos_maxage, lod.mdt_qos_maxage \- age of cached target free space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param lod." FSNAME "*.qos_maxage"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param lod." FSNAME "*.qos_maxage=" SECONDS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param lod." FSNAME "*.mdt_qos_maxage"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param lod." FSNAME "*.mdt_qos_maxage=" SECONDS
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Perms
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present on MDS nodes
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_maxage= 5
.br
.RB lod.*.mdt_qos_maxage= 5
.TP
.B Valid Range
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_maxage= 1
.br
.RB lod.*.qos_maxage= 4294967295
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qos_maxage
is how many seconds the MDS uses the free space and inodes of the OSTs
it has cached, before it asks the OSTs again, and
.B mdt_qos_maxage
is the same for the MDTs.
The free space decides whether new objects and directory stripes are
allocated in round-robin order or by free space, see
.BR lod.qos_threshold_rr (4)
and
.BR lod.qos_prio_free (4).
Setting it also sets the
.B maxage
of the OSP devices of the targets.
.PP
Shorter intervals follow the free space of the targets more closely, at
the cost of more statfs requests to them.
The penalties of recently used MDTs also decay in multiples of
.BR mdt_qos_maxage .
.SH EXAMPLES
Refresh the free space of the OSTs every 10 seconds on all MDTs of the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB "mds# " "lctl set_param lod.testfs-*.qos_maxage=10"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B qos_maxage
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.4.0, and
.B mdt_qos_maxage
since release 2.13.0.
Before that it was
.BR lov.qos_maxage ,
since release 1.8.0.
